  ],
  "secondary_categories": [],
  "slug": "structure-biological-process-8512",
  "summary": "Updated releases of established resources add evidence records, AI-assisted search, and gene-redundancy-aware catalogs for expert query.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is curated, evidence-linked reference resources that organize experimentally supported or literature-derived biological elements for expert query. ENdb 2.0 adds 4831 evidence records and TF-target links across five species, and tModBase v2.0 expands to 528 datasets across 23 species with an AI-powered assistant. EVLncRNAs 4.0 pairs curated functional lncRNAs with RAG-based search and PMID-linked citations. CellMarker 3.0 and CellMethMarker supply cell- and tissue-type markers for single-cell and deconvolution workflows, the latter comprising 347,514 de novo and 2.2M literature-derived methylation markers. RED 2.0 rebases rice expression onto the T2T Nipponbare reference. What is new is explicit treatment of gene redundancy: LoGIC catalogs local gene clusters whose homologs may compensate, and tWhEEL infers redundancy from transcripts to score CRISPR knockout feasibility.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-02"
}
